## Decision: In order to address this challenge service functions will be changed to the following pattern.

* The service function will receive the original command
* The command is then used to decide if another topic is broadcast to
* Another service function will be written to handle any data transformation
and the writing of the data to Firebase
* Tests for all service functions will be written
* Unit tests for the data transformation function will also be written

### Example

The following is an example of the above pattern being used

```javascript
/*
This function will receive the original command and will decide whether or not a message needs to be broadcast to another topic
*/
export function notifySubscribedUsersOfNewTask(payload, meta) {
  // We need to write a notification for every subscribed user. So we should loop over them
  return new Promise((resolve) => {
    // If the data does not include any users to notify then we can exit from the function
    if (!payload.users) {
      resolve();
    }

    payload.users.map((user) => {
      // The notification message needs to reference the user that it was created for
      const notification = Object.assign({}, payload);
      delete notification.users;
      notification.user = user;

      // Broadcast the new notification to the messaging queue
      return resolve(
        messenger.publish('notification.created', notification, meta)
      );
    });
  });
}

/*
This function performs all data transformation from the command and then stores the result in firebase
*/
export function storeNotificationInFirebase(payload) {
  // When saving a notification it needs to have an id and the current date it was stored on
  const notificationToSave = Object.assign({}, payload);
  notificationToSave.createdAt = new Date();
  notificationToSave.updatedAt = new Date();
  notificationToSave.isRead = false;

  // We are storing notifications in an array so need to retrieve them to add the new notification to the array
  const notifications = [];
  firebaseAdmin
    .database()
    .ref('notifications')
    .child(notificationToSave.user)
    .once('value', (snapshot) => {
      // Store all of the retrieved notifications to save
      const notificationsFromDb = snapshot.val();
      if (notificationsFromDb) {
        Object.keys(notificationsFromDb).map((notification) => {
          notifications.push(notificationsFromDb[notification]);
          return false;
        });
      }

      // Finally save the notification array to the database
      const key = firebaseAdmin
        .database()
        .ref()
        .push().key;
      notificationToSave.id = key;
      notifications.push(notificationToSave);
      return firebaseAdmin
        .database()
        .ref()
        .child(`notifications/${notificationToSave.user}`)
        .update(notifications);
    });
  return Promise.resolve(notificationToSave);
}
```

